      "granularity_name": "harmonic-family"
    },
    {
      "chord_quality": "dom7",
      "function_role": "upper-partials-extension-policy",
      "narrative": "Baker prescribes treating dom7 as the floor of a range of Upper Partial alterations: 'The dominant chord can be the dominant 7th, 9th, 11th, aug. 11th or 13th. The 5th or the 9th can be Flatted, nevertheless, these are still the Upper Partials of the dominant chord.' All extended dominant forms share the resolution function of the plain dom7. Chapter 10, p. 14.",
      "source_principle_ids": [
        "mickey-baker:complete-course-vol-2:functional-diatonic-harmony:upper-partials-dominant-alteration"
      ],
