      "granularity_name": "harmonic-family"
    },
    {
      "chord_quality": "dom11",
      "function_role": "harmonic-family-membership",
      "narrative": "Baker enumerates the 11th and augmented 11th as explicit members of the dominant's Upper Partials family: 'The dominant chord can be the dominant 7th, 9th, 11th, aug. 11th or 13th.' Dom11 and dom7#11 share the same resolution function and are treated as color variants, not structural departures. Chapter 10, p. 14.",
      "source_principle_ids": [
        "mickey-baker:complete-course-vol-2:functional-diatonic-harmony:upper-partials-dominant-alteration"
