    {
      "chord_quality": "dom13",
      "function_role": "harmonic-family-membership",
      "narrative": "Baker lists the 13th as the outermost Upper Partial of the dominant chord. G13b9 appears by name in the performance solo 'Just Bobi' (Chapter 29) and as the chord played over a G pedal in C Major at the Cadence Break (Chapter 22, p. 37: 'a Dm9 and a G13b9 chord play'). It resolves to the tonic on the same functional basis as all other dominant extensions. Chapter 10, p. 14; Chapter 22, p. 37.",
      "source_principle_ids": [
        "mickey-baker:complete-course-vol-2:functional-diatonic-harmony:upper-partials-dominant-alteration"
