    {
      "chord_quality": "dom7b9",
      "function_role": "pedal-point-upper-voice",
      "narrative": "Baker prescribes G13b9 as one of the specific chord variations played above a G pedal tone in the key of C Major: 'In exercise 56 \u2026 a Dm9 and a G13b9 chord play. This is the most popular form of Pedal Point.' The b9 coloring is explicitly named as the preferred upper-voice quality in this context. Chapter 22, p. 37.",
      "source_principle_ids": [
        "mickey-baker:complete-course-vol-2:counterpoint-chord-melody:pedal-point-fifth-canonical"
