    {
      "chord_quality": "min9",
      "function_role": "song-form-opening-chord",
      "narrative": "Baker prescribes opening chord-and-song-form exercises with the minor 9th and closing with the minor 6th: 'In both cases you are starting with the major or minor 9th and closing with the major or minor 6th.' The min9 is the structural opener; students practice this motion applied to well-known standard tunes. Chapter 7, p. 10.",
      "source_principle_ids": [
        "mickey-baker:complete-course-vol-2:functional-diatonic-harmony:ninth-to-sixth-voice-leading"
