    },
    {
      "chord_quality": "min9",
      "function_role": "pedal-point-upper-voice",
      "narrative": "Baker names Dm9 as one of the two specific chord variations played over a G pedal in C Major: 'In exercise 56 \u2026 a Dm9 and a G13b9 chord play. This is the most popular form of Pedal Point.' The min9 thus functions as the predominant color voice above the pedal fifth. Chapter 22, p. 37.",
      "source_principle_ids": [
        "mickey-baker:complete-course-vol-2:counterpoint-chord-melody:pedal-point-fifth-canonical"
