    },
    {
      "chord_quality": "min6",
      "function_role": "ninth-to-sixth-voice-leading-destination",
      "narrative": "Baker prescribes the minor 6th as the resolution target of the minor ninth via passing tones \u2014 'chord 1, through use of passing tones, resolves into chord 15 \u2026 moving from a minor ninth to a minor sixth chord, via passing tones.' The passing tones (marked 'P' in diagrams) are the voice-leading mechanism, and min6 is the harmonic goal of the minor-mode modern progression. Chapter 4, p. 7.",
      "source_principle_ids": [
        "mickey-baker:complete-course-vol-2:functional-diatonic-harmony:ninth-to-sixth-voice-leading"
      ],
