      "granularity_name": "idiom-application"
    },
    {
      "chord_quality": "maj9",
      "function_role": "ninth-to-sixth-voice-leading-source",
      "narrative": "Baker treats the major 9th as the parallel major-mode departure chord: 'Chords 3 and 4 are resolving into chords 16 and 17. Each chord is moving from a major ninth via passing tones, to a major sixth. The only difference in these two forms is the mode.' The maj9 opens the major-mode modern progression exactly as min9 opens its minor counterpart. Chapter 4, p. 7.",
      "source_principle_ids": [
        "mickey-baker:complete-course-vol-2:functional-diatonic-harmony:ninth-to-sixth-voice-leading"
