    {
      "chord_quality": "maj9",
      "function_role": "song-form-opening-chord",
      "narrative": "Baker prescribes the major 9th as the opening chord in major-mode song-form exercises, with the major 6th as its resolution: 'In both cases you are starting with the major or minor 9th and closing with the major or minor 6th.' Applied to standard tunes in Chapter 7, p. 10.",
      "source_principle_ids": [
