    {
      "chord_quality": "dim7",
      "function_role": "tonic-resolution-voice-leading",
      "narrative": "Baker prescribes that the diminished chord may replace the dominant in a V-I resolution: 'notice how the diminished chord instead of the dominant, resolves into the tonic. This is another form of the Altered chord.' Exercise 52 demonstrates the move extracted from a prior exercise, and the caption in Exercise 51 labels it 'the equivalent to the V - I Resolution.' Chapter 21, p. 34-35.",
      "source_principle_ids": [
        "mickey-baker:complete-course-vol-2:functional-diatonic-harmony:diminished-as-dominant-substitute"
      ],
