    {
      "chord_quality": "dim7",
      "function_role": "symmetric-harmony-tonic-vehicle",
      "narrative": "Baker designates the diminished 7th as the emblematic vehicle of Symmetric Harmony: 'a diminished 7th chord which moves freely up and down the finger board in minor thirds \u2026 A diminished chord is built on a succession of minor thirds \u2026 each tone in the chord is actually the root or the tonic.' Because all four inversions share the same pitch classes, the dim7 is the purest expression of the 4-tonic symmetric division. Chapter 13, p. 21.",
      "source_principle_ids": [
        "mickey-baker:complete-course-vol-2:symmetric-harmony:minor-third-symmetric-cycle"
      ],
